{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "inbound/a-binding-s-setting-is-read-as-pydantic-reads-it",
  "title": "An agent's turn reads the temperature and the max tokens its binding's metadata sets as pydantic's lax mode reads a float and an integer: a numeric text, a whole float, a boolean",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4",
    "Appendix A.9"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: channels/_ai_context.py _turn_settings hands the binding's values to AIContext(temperature: float, max_tokens: int | None), which pydantic validates in its lax mode: a float from a number, a boolean or a text that parses as one, blanks around it and underscores between digits taken; an integer from an integer, a boolean, a float with no fraction, or a text that parses as one, a fraction of zeros after it taken. room-1 '0.3' and '100'; room-2 1 and 64.0; room-3 true and false; room-4 ' 1e-1 ' and ' 1_000.00 '.",
  "setup": {
    "channels": [
      {
        "id": "sms",
        "type": "sms",
        "category": "transport"
      },
      {
        "id": "main",
        "type": "ai",
        "model": {
          "rounds": [
            {
              "text": "ok"
            },
            {
              "text": "ok"
            },
            {
              "text": "ok"
            },
            {
              "text": "ok"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "rooms": [
      {
        "id": "room-1",
        "bindings": [
          {
            "channel_id": "sms"
          },
          {
            "channel_id": "main",
            "category": "intelligence",
            "metadata": {
              "temperature": "0.3",
              "max_tokens": "100"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "room-2",
        "bindings": [
          {
            "channel_id": "sms"
          },
